===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=weblog|:from|weblog<id:Q30849>|tree=1}}
{{rebracketing|en|weblog}}, as if it means ''we blog''. The ''Oxford English Dictionary'' says the shortened word was coined 23 May 1999 and references the "Jargon Watch" article in an issue of an online magazine<ref>{{cite-web|last=Dawson|first=Keith|date=1999-08-30|url=http://tbtf.com/archive/1999-08-30.html#s10|title=TBTF for 1999-08-23: Compliance|accessdate=2012-01-02|work=Tasty Bits from the Technology Front|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260301025912/https://tbtf.com/archive/1999-08-30.html|archivedate=1 March 2026}}</ref> which attributes the shortening to Peter Merholz.<ref>{{cite-web|last=Merholz|first=Peter|date=2002-05-17|url=http://peterme.com/archives/00000205.html|title=Play With Your Words|accessdate=2012-01-02|work=peterme.com|passage=For What It's Worth: I've decided to pronounce the word 'weblog' as wee'- blog. Or 'blog' for short.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260710232722/https://peterme.com/archives/00000205.html|archivedate=10 July 2026}}</ref> The form ''blog'' is now so much more common than ''weblog'' that some misspell the latter as {{m|en|webblog}}, as if from ''web'' + ''blog''.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q30849}}{{lb|en|Internet}} A [[website]] that allows users to reflect, share opinions, and discuss various topics in the form of an online journal, sometimes letting readers comment on their [[post]]s. Most blogs are written in a slightly informal tone (personal journals, news, businesses, etc.)
#* {{quote-book|en|author=w:Biz Stone|chapter=1|title=Blogging: Genius Strategies for Instant Web Content|year=2002|location=Indianapolis|publisher=New Riders Pub.|page=4|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/blogging00bizs/page/4/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-7357-1299-7|passage=So you see, the '''blog''' has been around since the beginning of the web; that is how basic the concept is. Today's '''blogs''', and the activity of blogging, have taken on more meaning, but the concept of it all is still very simple and rooted in the beginning and intentions of the web itself.}}
#* {{RQ:Smith NW|page=150|passage=Have you tried these, darling? They’re tempura zucchini flowers. Japanese-Italian fusion! My own invention. Shall I photograph it? We can put it on our '''''blog'''''.}}
#* {{RQ:LATimes|url=https://www.latimes.com/local/lanow/la-me-ln-base-jumper-killed-20151002-story.html|title=BASE jumper Johnny Strange dies in wingsuit jump in Swiss Alps|date=2015-10-02|author=Veronica Rocha|passage=Potter addressed the dangers in a '''blog''' post.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20160201202228/https://www.latimes.com/local/lanow/la-me-ln-base-jumper-killed-20151002-story.html}}
# {{lb|en|Internet}} An individual post to a blog.
#: {{ux|en|This '''blog''' was originally posted on my personal site but is reproduced on the forums for greater visibility.}}

